# core.autocrlf is true in this repo, and git only auto-detects "binary" by
# looking for a NUL byte in a file's first 8000 bytes. An Illustrator/PDF
# file has none, so git would classify design/*.ai as TEXT and rewrite its
# line endings on checkout -- silently corrupting the logo master. Mark the
# binary asset types explicitly rather than relying on the heuristic.
*.ai binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
